# Shipped by the claude-code host component.
# homelab-claude-land@.service refuses an agent PR that changes, adds, deletes or renames out of a path
# under any prefix below, unless the operator approved its head. Plain prefixes, so
# `scripts/deploy_tools/land` covers land.sh, land.py and land_lib/. The modules the landing
# process imports are refused the same way, derived at landing time (land_lib/policy.py,
# gate_hits), so this list holds only what no import walk can see.
#
# DECIDED: a floor, not every path that widens the agent's authority (operator decision,
# 2026-10-10). It keeps the explicit grant points and the gate itself. The agent's roles, the
# deployer and the inventory land without approval. This is not a barrier to root: a host
# package installs any host component change as root, so a change in an unlisted component
# reaches root. That was already true under the wider list. docs/claude-agent-user.md, "The
# approval floor", has the reasoning. The list is literal here, not a variable, so the inventory cannot override it.
#
# The lander: this list, the unit that reads it, the rule that lets the agent start it, the
# template that pins the lander's name and settings, and the host component that ships them and
# decides when (H7.40's second slice).
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/claude-land-approval-paths.j2
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/claude-land@.service.j2
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/50-claude-land.rules.j2
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/claude-land-pins.j2
hosts/components/claude-code/component.yml
# Alert-triggered triage (operator decision, 2026-10-15): every claude-triage template (a
# prefix: the pins file that sets the run's caps and identity, the unit, its config, its prompt
# and its credential file, the poller's unit and timer), the polkit rule that lets the agent
# start a run, the runner and the poller. A run will land its own fixes with nobody watching,
# so it must not raise its own caps or arm its own trigger.
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/claude-triage
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/50-claude-triage.rules.j2
hosts/components/claude-code/files/claude_triage_run.py
hosts/components/claude-code/files/claude_triage_poll.py
# The read-only root inspector (issue #6323): the root script that decides what root reads and
# prints, the shim and the sudoers grant. The agent holds the grant, so it must not widen what
# the grant reaches.
hosts/components/claude-code/files/homelab_rootq.py
hosts/components/claude-code/files/rootq.sh
hosts/components/claude-code/templates/claude-rootq.sudoers.j2
# The same inspector through the agent's socket (#6350). The issue expected the entries above
